# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the C consumer sanitizer lane (C SDK plan,
# C5), read by run-c-consumers.py --sanitize.
#
# Policy: one entry per KNOWN, intentionally retained allocation class of
# libnet, each matched by a frame of its own allocation stack and each with
# its reason. Never a blanket `leak:libnet.so` — that would hide exactly the
# library-returned buffer the arming program leaks. The runner prints how
# many blocks and bytes each entry absorbed, per program, so a suppression
# is reported rather than hidden. Reachability from a static is not a claim
# that teardown reclaims it; nothing here claims that.
#
# Entries are added from real reports of the lane, never guessed.
